// TEST: Quantity Slot Rejects Bare Argument (rejects)
// ERROR: BL3010
// A parameter declared with a QUANTITY only accepts values ASSERTED to be
// that quantity: a bare literal must be ascribed at the call site
// (`twice((4.0 : speed))`). Structural-unit parameters keep the permissive
// behavior (units/002-008); the strictness is scoped to Nominal slots.
Unit meters
Unit seconds
Unit mps = meters / seconds
Unit speed: mps
function twice(x: Float<speed>) -> Float<speed> = x + x
let r = twice(4.0)
